    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Write personalised cold email opening lines for Google Sheets leads with AI\n\nTurn a sheet of leads into specific, non-cheesy first lines for your cold emails, written from the details you already have.\n\n### How it works\n1. Run it manually whenever you add leads.\n2. Leads with an email and an empty `status` are read from the **Leads** tab, up to `max_leads_per_run`.\n3. Gemini writes one opening line per lead, using only the facts in the row (company, role, website, notes), and says what it based the line on and how confident it is.\n4. The line, its basis and a status are written back to the same row, so each lead is only processed once.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet with a tab `Leads` and the columns `first_name, last_name, email, company, role, website, notes, first_line, first_line_basis, status`. The more you put in `notes` (a recent post, news, a detail from their site), the better the lines.\n2. Put the Sheet ID in **Set your offer** and add a **Google Sheets** credential.\n3. Add a **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential with a free key from aistudio.google.com.\n4. Describe your offer in **Set your offer** and click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the rules in **Write opening line with AI** for a different length or style.\n- Swap the Manual Trigger for a Schedule Trigger to process new leads daily.\n- Clear a lead's `status` to regenerate its line.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 936,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "e50f9436-c064-5772-8a55-cf0add18ca03",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -720,
        -150
      ]
    },
